<title>USA: Appliance Recycling increases credit line.</title>
<headline>Appliance Recycling increases credit line.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Appliance Recycling Centers of America Inc said Monday its line of credit has been expanded to $2 million from $1.5 million.</p>
<p>The increased line of credit is secured by receivables, inventory, equipment and real estate and will be used to support the company's national reconditioned appliance business, the company said.</p>
<p>Shares of Appliance Recycling, the nation's largest recycler of major household products, were up 1/64 at 1-9/64 on Nasdaq Monday.</p>
<p>--Reuters Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
